# Line-ending policy.
#
# The reason this file exists: Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`,
# which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout for anything it decides is text. It guesses
# wrong on PDFs — a byte that happens to be 0x0A inside a compressed stream becomes
# 0x0D 0x0A, the file grows, and the xref offsets no longer point where they claim.
# The result is `Could not read PDF: Unexpected EOF` on a fresh clone, which would
# take the whole parser suite down with it and make "git clone && pytest -q works"
# false on a default Windows install.
#
# Normalize text in the repository, and never touch binaries.

* text=auto

*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.traineddata binary
